{"id":"n-20261010-6vm4lp","category":"gaming","display_title":"Flanagan to Direct Warhammer 40,000 Series","display_title_he":"מייק פלנגן יביים את סדרת \"וורהאמר 40,000\"","short_summary":"Director Mike Flanagan has been chosen to helm Amazon's upcoming Warhammer 40,000 live-action series starring Henry Cavill.","english_level":"C1","words":465,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Polygon","domain":"polygon.com","url":"https://www.polygon.com/warhammer-40k-tv-series-henry-cavill-mike-flanagan","title":"Henry Cavill's New Sci-fi Streaming Series Sets Carrie Reboot Creator to Direct","published_at":"2026-10-10T21:06:47.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-10T21:06:47.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-10T22:05:19.618Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The bleak and dystopian universe of Warhammer 40,000 is moving closer to a major live-action screen adaptation, with seasoned horror filmmaker Mike Flanagan attached to direct. A financial report published by Games Workshop, the creator of the popular tabletop wargame, confirmed that Amazon and United Artists have selected Flanagan to helm the ambitious project starring British actor Henry Cavill. According to Games Workshop Chief Executive Officer Kevin Rountree, Flanagan has already completed initial narrative outlines for the series and is expected to transition into writing the formal scripts shortly.","Flanagan’s appointment brings a distinguished pedigree in dark, psychological storytelling to the franchise. Over recent years, the director has earned widespread critical acclaim for crafting chilling horror adaptations and original television series, including Netflix hits such as The Haunting of Hill House, The Haunting of Bly Manor, Midnight Mass, and The Fall of the House of Usher. His directorial portfolio also features notable cinematic adaptations of Stephen King literature, such as Gerald’s Game and Doctor Sleep, alongside a forthcoming Prime Video adaptation of Carrie and a project centered on the DC Comics villain Clayface.","For dedicated enthusiasts of the tabletop universe, the corporate report provides reassuring confirmation regarding Henry Cavill’s continued involvement. Cavill, a self-proclaimed, passionate fan of the lore and miniatures game, remains firmly attached to the live-action venture. Warhammer 40,000, which helped popularize the brooding sci-fi subgenre known as \"grimdark,\" presents a brutal vision of the far future. In this setting, humanity’s relentless interstellar expansion has plunged civilization into perpetual warfare against hostile alien species, cosmic horrors, and corrupting chaos. Bringing such an expansive and intricate mythos to television carries immense expectations from a loyal global fanbase.","Nevertheless, patience will be required before the live-action production reaches global audiences. Games Workshop explicitly noted in its corporate financial report that bringing these complex adaptations to market successfully will take several years. Notably, Rountree’s reference to \"adaptations\" in the plural strongly suggests that the strategic partnership with Amazon encompasses multiple media projects rather than a singular television series or standalone feature film.","In the interim, fans of Games Workshop's intellectual properties have several animated endeavors to look forward to. Rountree disclosed that the company has nearly finished work on an animated episode for the second season of the Secret Level anthology series. Unlike its previous installment, this upcoming episode will be set within the Age of Sigmar universe, the fantasy counterpart to Warhammer 40,000.","Furthermore, work has officially begun on a dedicated animated Warhammer 40,000 series featuring the Space Marines unit known as Deathwatch. That animated project is currently being written by screenwriter John Orloff, with animation duties again handled by Blur Studio, and will eventually be released through Amazon. Together, these complementary projects signify a calculated effort to translate Games Workshop’s iconic tabletop mythos onto mainstream digital streaming platforms."],"facts":[{"fact":"Games Workshop confirmed in a financial report that Amazon assigned United Artists and director Mike Flanagan to helm the Warhammer 40,000 Prime Video adaptation starring Henry Cavill.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Games Workshop CEO Kevin Rountree stated that Flanagan has completed initial outlines and will soon begin writing scripts.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Flanagan has previously directed horror projects like Netflix's The Haunting of Hill House, Midnight Mass, and The Fall of the House of Usher, as well as Stephen King adaptations like Gerald's Game and Doctor Sleep, and is working on Carrie and DC's Clayface.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Henry Cavill, a devoted fan of Warhammer 40,000, remains attached to star in the project.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Games Workshop noted that the adaptations will take years to bring to market, hinting at multiple projects due to the plural usage of 'adaptations'.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Games Workshop is almost finished with an episode for Secret Level Season 2 set in the Age of Sigmar fantasy universe.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Work has begun on a full animated Warhammer 40,000 series centered on the Space Marines Deathwatch, written by John Orloff, animated by Blur, and to be released via Amazon.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"bleak","lemma":"bleak","pos":"adjective","he":"קודר, עגום","name":false},{"text":"dystopian","lemma":"dystopian","pos":"adjective","he":"דיסטופי","name":false},{"text":"universe","lemma":"universe","pos":"noun","he":"יקום","name":false},{"text":"Warhammer 40,000","lemma":"Warhammer 40,000","pos":"name","he":"וורהאמר 40,000","name":true},{"text":"moving closer","lemma":"move closer","pos":"phrasal verb","he":"מתקרב","name":false},{"text":"live-action","lemma":"live-action",